name wordframenet-wfn
# WFN/WordFrameNet: each frame header scopes its lexical rows, including
# rows separated by blank lines. Source: adimen.ehu.eus/web/WordFrameNet;
# Laparra/Rigau RANLP2009, table 1 (WordNet 1.6 offsets, not PWN3.0 keys).
match WordFrameNet
format frame_lexicon

thing frame header/name
type header.name fnframe node
content *
# A reference retains both its numeric offset and syntactic category, qualified
# by the edition the source used. It is not a guessed ILI/highway crosswalk.
thing reference literal WordNet literal 1.6 offset category
# Reuse the lexical-sense composition used by the WordNet recipes: surface,
# language and concept. The English language is declared by the source paper.
# WordNet's lexical spelling writes underscores for spaces.
thing lexicalization preserve spelling space _ literal eng ^entry/reference
# Each row is one alignment, with any source annotation and definition kept
# in that context. The pipe-form row's numeric annotation is never a score.
thing entry resolved preserve ^frame/header/name required lexicalization required pos required annotation definition
itself entry
